<title>USA: HIGH PLAINS WHEAT - SCATTERED PROTECTION TAKEN.</title>
<headline>HIGH PLAINS WHEAT - SCATTERED PROTECTION TAKEN.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scattered two to three cents per bushel protection was being taken Monday morning on hard red winter wheat in Kansas, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the protection was being taken amid lower opening calls for KCBT wheat futures. They said wheat will likely see opening pressure from CBOT corn and soybeans, which were called lower after beneficial rains fell over the weekend in some dry growing areas of Illinois and Indiana.</p>
<p>The protection on wheat was limited to a few locations in Kansas. Dealers in Oklahoma said they were not taking protection on wheat.  </p>
